{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01SXmR9XmKY9x9AXyKgRcr1c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! So **\"prospero\" IS in \"the prince prospero\"** - the substring check SHOULD work. This means the issue MUST be in the `_validate_merge()` rejection.\n\nLet me update my root cause analysis and add targeted diagnostic logging:\n\n## ROOT CAUSE IDENTIFIED\n\nThe substring pre-merge logic (attempt 17) is correct:\n- `\"prospero\"` IS a substring of `\"the prince prospero\"` ✓\n- The pre-merge phase iterates through names before LLM evaluation ✓\n\n**BUT:** The `_validate_merge()` call at line 1080 is REJECTING the merge!\n\nLooking at the validation logic (lines 1511-1750), the most likely rejection point is:\n\n**Lines 1681-1686: Ambiguous last name rejection**\n```python\n# If one is just a last name, it's ambiguous - reject\nif len(words1) == 1 or len(words2) == 1:\n    logger.debug(\n        f\"Merge rejected: {canonical} <-> {alias} \"\n        f\"(ambiguous last name with multiple family members: {names_with_lastname})\"\n    )\n    return False, 0.2\n```\n\nThis check triggers when:\n1. Names share a word that's a last name (both end with same word)\n2. Multiple full names exist with that last name\n3. One name is single-word\n\nIn this case:\n- \"Prospero\" (single word)\n- \"the Prince Prospero\" (has \"Prospero\" as last name)\n- Multiple names might have \"Prospero\" (e.g., \"Prospero\", \"Prince Prospero\", \"the Prince Prospero\")\n\n**This is the ROOT CAUSE!** The ambiguous last name check is incorrectly rejecting the valid substring match."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":46829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":649,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59295c31-f08f